      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T21:59:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A nit really but isn\u0027t there a way to write these without having to use indices that could easily get out of sync? We know that we\u0027re writing a uint16 starting at the next position.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 892,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 892,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "01918a14da74a9799bf3c2734276664bb95b3236",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c2808c73_ec7fcb19",
        "filename": "zip/zip.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 892,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T23:53:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could make the array with a size of 0 and a capacity of `4+dataSize`, then use `binary.LittleEndian.AppendUint16` for each field, but that adds a few risks.  First is that it makes it easy to accidentally change the binary format.  Second is that the capacity is not a limit, so a modification might cause append to exceed your expected `dataSize`.  Those risks are somewhat mitigated by the tests though.\n\nYou can see how the stdlib does it at https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:prebuilts/go/linux-x86/src/archive/zip/writer.go;l\u003d109-117;drc\u003d31b9b84cf8ff78b0f713c11d813c70dd456a018d, which is pretty similar to what is done here with a little extra wrapper that tracks the write position in the buffer",
      "parentUuid": "cc8f533f_527098fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 892,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 892,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "01918a14da74a9799bf3c2734276664bb95b3236",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "676f1832_b72a8d85",
        "filename": "zip/zip.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 892,
      "author": {
        "id": 1480888
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T00:54:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, a wrapper that took a Writer and buffer was sort of what I was thinking. I was hoping that Go had native support for it without having to write a custom class.\n\nMaybe this?\n\n```\nbuffer :\u003d new(bytes.Buffer)\nbinary.Write(buffer, binary.LittleEndian, Sha256HeaderID)\nbinary.Write(buffer, binary.LittleEndian, uint16(dataSize))\n...\n\nze.fh.Extra \u003d append(ze.fh.Extra, buf.Bytes()...)\n```\n\nSee https://pkg.go.dev/encoding/binary#example-Write-Multi.",
      "parentUuid": "c2808c73_ec7fcb19",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 892,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 892,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "01918a14da74a9799bf3c2734276664bb95b3236",
